Everything works. Here's the summary:

| Goal | API | Returns |
|------|-----|---------|
| Strongly-typed metadata | `options.GetTypeInfo<T>()` | `JsonTypeInfo<T>` directly — no cast |
| Probe without throwing | `options.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(T), out JsonTypeInfo? info)` | `bool` — `false` if unavailable |

Both were introduced in .NET 9 and are available on your `net11.0` target. The key file:

```csharp
// Typed retrieval
JsonTypeInfo<Person> typedInfo = options.GetTypeInfo<Person>();

// Safe probe
if (options.TryGetTypeInfo(typeof(Person), out JsonTypeInfo? found))
    // use found
else
    // not available — no exception
```
